<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Q'eqchi' people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kekchi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Q'eqchi' are a Maya people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a> and Belize, centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alta-verapaz">Alta Verapaz</a> and spreading into Izabal, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peten">Petén</a> and southern Belize. Their language, Q'eqchi', is one of the most widely spoken Mayan languages, with more than a million speakers. From the late nineteenth century much of their land was taken for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> plantations, and many migrated north into the lowland forests.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qeqchi-people.jpg" alt="Q'eqchi' people" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Infrogmation of New Orleans · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CobanAVPJovenes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
